To find $A$ and $B$, we take the following equation and multiply both sides by the common denominator:

$\begin{align}
\displaystyle\dfrac{x+5}{(x+2)(x-1)}&=\dfrac{A}{x+2}+\dfrac{B}{x-1}
\\\\
\displaystyle {x+5}&={A(x-1)}+{B(x+2)}
\end{align}$

Substituting $x=-2$, we get $\blueD{A=-1}$.

Substituting $x=1$, we get $\maroonD{B=2}$.
